ith me about it  it's the emotionally charged moments in  between that left a lasting impression  the ones that leverage my enduring love  of the character a my familiarity with  the world but placed me at the heart of  it there's a bit where I lowered the  cowl over my face then looked in the  mirror and saw Batman staring back at me  it was a moment that gave me pause and  despite knowing I'm a grown  standing in a dark room with an absurd  looking virtual reality headset strapped  to my face I believed I was Batman for a  moment I was transporting to Gotham see  and I was his greatest hero as I was  lowered deeper on the ground  the metallic elevator gave way to a vast  Kevin bats fluttered through the air  their screeches just barely piercing  through the sound of crashing waterfalls  to my left was the t-rex statue from my  adventure on dinosaur island on the  right was the giant penny that marks my  tussle with the penny plunderer I was in  the Batcave and it was overwhelming I  had seen this place countless times over  my lifetime but never like this never  from this perspective  [Music]  please select vehicle in the bat-cave  garage a summoned the Batmobile and  emerged on a platform stopping right in  front of my face I could finally see  what the Joker twoface and the many  thoughts in Gotham so whenever Batman  rocketed through the streets in pursuit  of villainy and at the touch of a button  it transformed from the nimble pursuit  mode into the tank-like battle mode it  was majestic imposing powerful Arkham VI  also let me get up close with heroes and  villains that I had only seen on flat  planes up until that point I could see  every detail in Nightwing chiseled jaw  and his ripped gymnast physique or the  gruesome appearance of villains that  shalt be named and the alley I was  carefully scouring in stark corners and  soaking up that grimy Gotham atmosphere  that I'd read so much about I stared up  into the sky at the iconic Batman symbol  projected onto the clouds and it made me  smile Batman Arkham VR is barely a game  of all the launch titles for PlayStation  VR it's likely to be the least  mechanically driven but that doesn't  mean it has no value  while playing it I was totally enveloped  in the world and in those moments the  shallow mechanics didn't matter to me I  appreciate that this is a subjective  emotional response based on my lifelong  obsession with the character but it's  also a glimpse into one of the greatest  promises of VR its ability to transport  us into alien worlds and blur the lines  between what's real and what isn't  to give us the opportunity for style and  our real selves and absolutely inhabit  characters we've dreamed of being since  childhood  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]

